 "equipment_type": "In-row precision cooling unit (computer room air handler)",
 "applies_to": "Liebert CRV in-row cooling units with the iCOM v4 controller.",
 "summary": "The Liebert CRV in-row cooling reports to a BMS through a Liebert IntelliSlot card (IS-UNITY-DP for BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP; some units also IS-IPBML). The object list has Binary Values for events, Analog Values for temperatures, humidity, setpoints and run hours, and Multi-state Values for states and control modes. Objects are created on the card when it discovers the unit, so only options fitted to the unit appear.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Tables 5.22, 5.23, 5.24, 5.25, pdf pages 1421-1432 of the 2024 guide (printed page numbers are 4 lower).",
  "Object names are Vertiv data IDs (e.g. 5331_1); the description holds the guide's data label. Labels repeated for different sensors or circuits get the group name in brackets.",
  "Most temperature objects come in pairs: a °C object and a °F object (name ending _deg_F), usually at instance + 10000."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "Liebert IntelliSlot Modbus/BACnet Reference Guide (Modbus RTU and TCP, BACnet MSTP and IP)",
  "doc_number": "SL-28170",
